```

## Age 65: the day before the birthday

Pub. 501 (2024) p 3: "A person is considered to reach age 65 on the day before
the person's 65th birthday." Born 1960-01-01: reaches 65 on 2024-12-31, so
65 or older for TY2024. Born 1960-01-02: reaches 65 on 2025-01-01, so not.
Born 1959-12-31: 65 on 2024-12-30, so yes.

The plain age of the person born 1960-01-01 is 64. A rule that used the plain
age (`primary_age >= 65`) would give the wrong answer, and the last assertion
rejects it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAge65:
  output ok condition
  jan1 scope Case
  jan2 scope Case
  dec31 scope Case

scope TestAge65:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition jan1.primary_dob equals |1960-01-01|
  definition jan2.primary_dob equals |1960-01-02|
  definition dec31.primary_dob equals |1959-12-31|
  assertion jan1.primary_age65
  assertion not jan2.primary_age65
  assertion dec31.primary_age65
  assertion jan1.primary_age = 64
  assertion jan2.primary_age = 64
  assertion dec31.primary_age = 65
  # Known-bad output: the plain-age rule disagrees with the spec for Jan 1, 1960.
  assertion jan1.primary_age65 != (jan1.primary_age >= 65)
```

An independent reference for the same rule, the Pub. 501 wording "65th birthday
on or before January 1 of the following year" (DF `/filers/*/age65OrOlder`
description, `filers.xml` line 648), checked on dates around the boundary.

```catala
declaration scope Pub501Age65:
  input date_of_birth content date
  output is_65 condition

scope Pub501Age65:
  definition is_65 equals date_of_birth + 65 year <= |2025-01-01|

#[test]
declaration scope TestAge65Reference:
  output ok condition
  a scope Case
  b scope Case
  c scope Case
  d scope Case
  e scope Case
  ra scope Pub501Age65
  rb scope Pub501Age65
  rc scope Pub501Age65
  rd scope Pub501Age65
  re scope Pub501Age65

scope TestAge65Reference:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition a.primary_dob equals |1959-12-31|
  definition b.primary_dob equals |1960-01-01|
  definition c.primary_dob equals |1960-01-02|
  definition d.primary_dob equals |1960-07-04|
  definition e.primary_dob equals |1930-02-28|
  definition ra.date_of_birth equals |1959-12-31|
  definition rb.date_of_birth equals |1960-01-01|
  definition rc.date_of_birth equals |1960-01-02|
  definition rd.date_of_birth equals |1960-07-04|
  definition re.date_of_birth equals |1930-02-28|
  assertion a.primary_age65 = ra.is_65
  assertion b.primary_age65 = rb.is_65
  assertion c.primary_age65 = rc.is_65
  assertion d.primary_age65 = rd.is_65
  assertion e.primary_age65 = re.is_65
```

## Earned Income Credit age: 25 on the day before, 64 on the actual birthday

Pub. 596 (2024) p 16: "You meet the age test if you were born after December
31, 1959, and before January 2, 2000." Born 2000-01-01: reaches 25 on
1999-12-31, so meets the minimum. Born 2000-01-02: does not. For the maximum,
the person born 1960-01-01 reaches 65 on the actual birthday 2025-01-01, so
they are still "64 or younger" at the end of 2024 (and 65 or older for the
standard deduction); the person born 1959-12-31 is not.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEitcAge:
  output ok condition
  min_ok scope Case
  min_bad scope Case
  min_other scope Case
  max_ok scope Case
  max_ok_jan2 scope Case
  max_bad scope Case

scope TestEitcAge:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition min_ok.primary_dob equals |2000-01-01|
  definition min_bad.primary_dob equals |2000-01-02|
  definition min_other.primary_dob equals |1999-12-31|
  definition max_ok.primary_dob equals |1960-01-01|
  definition max_ok_jan2.primary_dob equals |1960-01-02|
  definition max_bad.primary_dob equals |1959-12-31|
  # minimum age 25: day-before rule
  assertion min_ok.primary_age25_for_eitc
  assertion not min_bad.primary_age25_for_eitc
  assertion min_other.primary_age25_for_eitc
  # maximum age 64: actual birthday
  assertion max_ok.primary_age64_for_eitc
  assertion max_ok.primary_age65
  assertion max_ok_jan2.primary_age64_for_eitc
  assertion not max_bad.primary_age64_for_eitc
  # a person born 1960-01-01 is 65 for the standard deduction but not too old for EITC
  assertion max_ok.primary_age65 and max_ok.primary_age64_for_eitc
```

## Spouse who died during the year

Pub. 596 p 16, Example 2: "Your spouse was born on February 14, 1999, and died
on February 13, 2024. Your spouse is considered age 25 at the time of death.
However, if your spouse died on February 12, 2024, your spouse isn't considered
age 25 at the time of death and isn't at least age 25 at the end of 2024."

Pub. 501 p 3: the deceased spouse is 65 for the standard deduction only if
65 at death, counting the day before the birthday. A spouse born 1959-07-10
reaches 65 on 2024-07-09: death on 2024-07-09 counts, on 2024-07-08 does not.
For the EITC maximum age the spouse reaches 65 on the actual birthday
(2024-07-10), so a death on 2024-07-09 still meets "under age 65".

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDeceasedSpouse:
  output ok condition
  age25_yes scope Case
  age25_no scope Case
  age65_yes scope Case
  age65_no scope Case

scope TestDeceasedSpouse:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition age25_yes.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition age25_yes.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition age25_yes.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedInTaxYear
  definition age25_yes.secondary_dob equals |1999-02-14|
  definition age25_yes.secondary_date_of_death equals |2024-02-13|
  definition age25_no.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition age25_no.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition age25_no.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedInTaxYear
  definition age25_no.secondary_dob equals |1999-02-14|
  definition age25_no.secondary_date_of_death equals |2024-02-12|
  definition age65_yes.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition age65_yes.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition age65_yes.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedInTaxYear
  definition age65_yes.secondary_dob equals |1959-07-10|
  definition age65_yes.secondary_date_of_death equals |2024-07-09|
  definition age65_no.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition age65_no.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition age65_no.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedInTaxYear
  definition age65_no.secondary_dob equals |1959-07-10|
  definition age65_no.secondary_date_of_death equals |2024-07-08|
  assertion age25_yes.treat_as_mfj
  assertion age25_yes.secondary_age25_for_eitc
  assertion not age25_no.secondary_age25_for_eitc
  assertion age65_yes.deceased_spouse_reached_age65
  assertion not age65_no.deceased_spouse_reached_age65
  assertion age65_yes.secondary_age64_for_eitc
```

## Marital status, residency and the joint return

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMarital:
  output ok condition
  married_mfj scope Case
  married_nra_spouse scope Case
  widowed_prior_year scope Case
  never_married scope Case

scope TestMarital:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition married_mfj.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition married_mfj.marital_status equals Married
  definition married_nra_spouse.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition married_nra_spouse.marital_status equals Married
  definition married_nra_spouse.secondary_is_citizen equals false
  definition widowed_prior_year.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition widowed_prior_year.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition widowed_prior_year.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedTaxYearMinusOne
  definition never_married.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  assertion married_mfj.eligible_for_mfj and married_mfj.treat_as_mfj
  # IRC 6013(a)(1): no joint return with a nonresident alien spouse
  assertion not married_nra_spouse.eligible_for_mfj
  assertion not married_nra_spouse.treat_as_mfj
  # widowed in an earlier year: not married at the end of the year (IRC 7703(a)(1))
  assertion not widowed_prior_year.eligible_for_mfj
  assertion not widowed_prior_year.treat_as_mfj
  # Known-bad: an MFJ status chosen by a never-married filer does not count
  assertion not never_married.treat_as_mfj
```

## Lived apart

IRC 7703(b)(3): the spouse "is not a member of such household" during the last
six months. DF derives it from the answers (`filers.xml` lines 3963 to 4102).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestLivedApart:
  output ok condition
  together_all_year scope Case
  apart_all_year scope Case
  together_more_than_six scope Case
  six_or_less_apart scope Case
  six_or_less_not_apart_agreement scope Case

scope TestLivedApart:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition together_all_year.marital_status equals Married
  definition apart_all_year.marital_status equals Married
  definition apart_all_year.lived_together_all_year equals false
  definition apart_all_year.lived_together_months equals LivedApartAllYear
  definition together_more_than_six.marital_status equals Married
  definition together_more_than_six.lived_together_all_year equals false
  definition together_more_than_six.lived_together_months equals
    LivedTogetherMoreThanSixMonths
  definition together_more_than_six.lived_apart_last_six_months equals true
  definition six_or_less_apart.marital_status equals Married
  definition six_or_less_apart.lived_together_all_year equals false
  definition six_or_less_apart.lived_together_months equals
    LivedTogetherSixMonthsOrLess
  definition six_or_less_apart.lived_apart_last_six_months equals true
  definition six_or_less_not_apart_agreement.marital_status equals Married
  definition six_or_less_not_apart_agreement.lived_together_all_year equals false
  definition six_or_less_not_apart_agreement.lived_together_months equals
    LivedTogetherSixMonthsOrLess
  definition six_or_less_not_apart_agreement.lived_apart_last_six_months equals false
  definition six_or_less_not_apart_agreement.separation_agreement equals true
  assertion not together_all_year.lived_apart_last_six
  assertion not together_all_year.filer_could_qualify_for_hoh
  assertion apart_all_year.lived_apart_last_six
  assertion apart_all_year.filer_could_qualify_for_hoh
  # the stale writable answer is ignored when the spouses lived together more than six months
  assertion not together_more_than_six.lived_apart_last_six
  assertion six_or_less_apart.lived_apart_last_six
  assertion not six_or_less_not_apart_agreement.lived_apart_last_six
  assertion six_or_less_not_apart_agreement.special_rule_for_separated_spouses
```

## Claimed as a dependent

`/treatFilersAsDependents` (`filers.xml` line 1441). Not joint: the filer can
be claimed and the claimer must file, or did file for more than a refund. Joint:
`/isMFJDependent` needs one spouse who can be claimed, a couple not required to
file, and a choice of refund only.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDependents:
  output ok condition
  must_file scope Case
  refund_only scope Case
  not_claimable scope Case
  filed_for_credits scope Case
  mfj_refund_only scope Case
  mfj_for_credits scope Case
  mfj_required scope Case

scope TestDependents:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition must_file.primary_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition must_file.primary_will_be_claimed equals true
  definition must_file.primary_claimer_must_file equals true
  definition refund_only.primary_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition refund_only.primary_will_be_claimed equals true
  definition refund_only.primary_claimer_must_file equals false
  definition refund_only.primary_claimer_did_file equals true
  definition refund_only.claimer_filed_only_for_refund equals true
  definition not_claimable.primary_claimer_must_file equals true
  definition filed_for_credits.primary_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition filed_for_credits.primary_will_be_claimed equals true
  definition filed_for_credits.primary_claimer_did_file equals true
  definition mfj_refund_only.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_refund_only.marital_status equals Married
  definition mfj_refund_only.secondary_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition mfj_refund_only.secondary_will_be_claimed equals true
  definition mfj_refund_only.mfj_required_to_file equals false
  definition mfj_refund_only.mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits equals false
  definition mfj_for_credits.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_for_credits.marital_status equals Married
  definition mfj_for_credits.secondary_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition mfj_for_credits.secondary_will_be_claimed equals true
  definition mfj_for_credits.mfj_required_to_file equals false
  definition mfj_for_credits.mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits equals true
  definition mfj_required.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_required.marital_status equals Married
  definition mfj_required.secondary_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition mfj_required.secondary_will_be_claimed equals true
  definition mfj_required.mfj_required_to_file equals true
  assertion must_file.treat_filers_as_dependents
  assertion not refund_only.treat_filers_as_dependents
  assertion not not_claimable.treat_filers_as_dependents
  assertion filed_for_credits.treat_filers_as_dependents
  assertion mfj_refund_only.is_mfj_dependent
  assertion mfj_refund_only.treat_filers_as_dependents
  assertion not mfj_refund_only.taxpayer_cannot_be_claimed
  assertion not mfj_for_credits.is_mfj_dependent
  assertion not mfj_for_credits.treat_filers_as_dependents
  assertion mfj_for_credits.taxpayer_cannot_be_claimed
  assertion not mfj_required.is_mfj_dependent
  assertion not mfj_required.treat_filers_as_dependents
```

