## Oldest filer

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMinimumDob:
  output ok condition
  joint scope Case
  single scope Case

scope TestMinimumDob:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition joint.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition joint.marital_status equals Married
  definition joint.primary_dob equals |1985-06-15|
  definition joint.secondary_dob equals |1980-03-01|
  definition single.primary_dob equals |1985-06-15|
  definition single.secondary_dob equals |1980-03-01|
  assertion joint.minimum_filer_date_of_birth = |1980-03-01|
  assertion single.minimum_filer_date_of_birth = |1985-06-15|
```

## From dates of birth to the standard deduction (Form 1040 line 12)

TY2024: single $14,600, MFJ $29,200, additional $1,950 (unmarried) or $1,550
(married) per item (Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.15). The age comes from the date of
birth through `Filers`.

- Single born 1960-01-01: 65 on 2024-12-31, $14,600 + $1,950 = $16,550.
- Single born 1960-01-02: not 65, $14,600.
- MFJ, both born 1960-01-01: $29,200 + 2 x $1,550 = $32,300.
- MFJ widowed in 2024, spouse born 1959-07-10 died 2024-07-09 (65 at death):
  primary born 1985, $29,200 + $1,550 = $30,750; died 2024-07-08: $29,200.
- Single who can be claimed and whose claimer must file, earned income $3,000:
  `GreaterOf($1,300, $3,000 + $450)` = $3,450.
- MFJ "refund only" dependent couple: the dependent minimum applies to the
  couple, `max($1,300, $50,000 + $450)` is above $29,200, so $29,200.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestStandardDeductionWiring:
  output ok condition
  single65 scope Case
  single64 scope Case
  mfj_both65 scope Case
  widow_died_65 scope Case
  widow_died_64 scope Case
  dependent scope Case
  mfj_dependent_couple scope Case

scope TestStandardDeductionWiring:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition single65.primary_dob equals |1960-01-01|
  definition single64.primary_dob equals |1960-01-02|
  definition mfj_both65.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_both65.marital_status equals Married
  definition mfj_both65.primary_dob equals |1960-01-01|
  definition mfj_both65.secondary_dob equals |1960-01-01|
  definition widow_died_65.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition widow_died_65.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition widow_died_65.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedInTaxYear
  definition widow_died_65.secondary_dob equals |1959-07-10|
  definition widow_died_65.secondary_date_of_death equals |2024-07-09|
  definition widow_died_64.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition widow_died_64.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition widow_died_64.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedInTaxYear
  definition widow_died_64.secondary_dob equals |1959-07-10|
  definition widow_died_64.secondary_date_of_death equals |2024-07-08|
  definition dependent.primary_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition dependent.primary_will_be_claimed equals true
  definition dependent.primary_claimer_must_file equals true
  definition dependent.employer_income_subtotal equals $3,000
  definition mfj_dependent_couple.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_dependent_couple.marital_status equals Married
  definition mfj_dependent_couple.secondary_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition mfj_dependent_couple.secondary_will_be_claimed equals true
  definition mfj_dependent_couple.mfj_required_to_file equals false
  definition mfj_dependent_couple.mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits equals false
  assertion single65.standard_deduction = $16,550
  assertion single64.standard_deduction = $14,600
  assertion mfj_both65.standard_deduction = $32,300
  assertion widow_died_65.standard_deduction = $30,750
  assertion widow_died_64.standard_deduction = $29,200
  assertion dependent.standard_deduction = $3,450
  assertion mfj_dependent_couple.standard_deduction = $29,200
```
